  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 4.5.1, 'Considerations for designing a digital health enterprise'. A checklist of five ticked considerations, each with guiding questions. Identified pain points and health system challenges: what challenges did the stakeholders identify, and are digital interventions appropriate or should non-digital approaches also be considered? Evidence base and experience with the digital health intervention(s): has it been shown to address the challenges, will more than one be needed, and has it been tested at the necessary scale? Enabling environment: can the enabling and ICT environment support it, and what precautions are needed (see Chapter 5)? Requirements: how well does the enterprise meet user needs and stakeholder expectations, and does it fit the existing culture, language and workflows? Linkages to other ICT enterprises: are other interventions being implemented in the context, and can they be leveraged?",
      "state": "draft",
